# Smoke Coverage Audit — Part 1: Inventory & Classification

File: openOODA/audit/smoke_coverage_audit_part1.oot
Logline: Enumerates the 12,478 std/ modules and fixture inventory, classifying baseline smoke coverage and real vs stub tests.

Setup: Run date 2026-08-28 (HST) from /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/ooda. Audit captured both pre-cleanup and post-cleanup states.

Beats:
  1. Module and fixture inventory across 209 std/ subtrees.
  2. Hand-written real smoke fixtures catalogue (20 fixtures).
  3. Baseline domain coverage rollup.
  4. Adversarial import stub classification (30 modules).

What this proves:
  * Only 20 of 12,478 modules (0.16%) have a real hand-written smoke test; 12,458 (99.84%) have at most a stub.
  * The highest-leverage Wave 2 work is concentrated in ~10 domains: crypto, math, net, encoding, collections.

