1.2  Fixture inventory
    Pre-cleanup:  $ ls fixtures/*_smoke.oo | wc -l
                  12507
    Post-cleanup: $ ls fixtures/*_smoke.oo | wc -l
                  59

    Pre-cleanup classification (12,507 files):

        10,927  First-generation stubs (file size < 1000 bytes)
                  Pattern: "VALID + NEGATIVE TRUST + ADVERSARIAL +
                  DOUBLE-RUN" boilerplate, call shim_marker_identity()
                  or <module>_<topic>_marker() or init_<module>_cfg(),
                  and println("OK: ..."). No assertions.
         1,560  First-generation stubs (1000–1500 bytes)
                  Same boilerplate, slightly longer per-module
                  comment header. Still no assertions.
            20  Hand-written real smoke fixtures (>=1000 bytes,
                  contain expect_eq / expect_true / expect_false /
                  FAIL: / process_exit(1) on assertion failure or
                  compare against a known-answer test vector).

    Post-cleanup classification (59 files): the 12,487 first-
    generation stubs were removed; the cleanup missed 24
    second-generation "adversarial import" stubs (a different
    vibe pattern, see part 5) that survived.

            20  Hand-written real smoke fixtures — see 1.3.
            24  Second-generation "adversarial import" stubs
                  that the parallel cleanup missed. Pattern:
                  "VALID import + NEGATIVE TRUST parse +
                  ADVERSARIAL context + DOUBLE-RUN" comment,
                  body is just `import "std/<path>.oo"; pub fn
                  main() { println("OK: ...") }`. They verify
                  only that the module compiles, not that it
                  works. See part 5 for the module list.
            15  Backend smoke tests (aarch64, x86, wasm
                  interpreter): test the compiler backends, not
                  std modules. Excluded from the std coverage
                  rollup.

